{0 Supported libraries}

This page gives examples of OCaml standard library features and libraries you
can use in a Worker. The list is not complete. A successful wasm_of_ocaml build
alone does not show that every function works in the Workers runtime. Check
each feature your code calls, especially if it needs operating system features
such as sockets or processes. Dependencies add to the Worker bundle. See
{{!page-limits}Limits}.

{1 Features in the example worker}

The routes in [examples/features/main.mlx] demonstrate these features. The
example builds a Worker; the repository test suite does not run these routes.
Test the routes you use in [workerd] and in your deployment:

- Effects: OCaml 5 effect handlers; a separate route awaits a Promise.
- [Hashtbl], [Lazy], [Seq], [Printexc] and [Random.State].
- [Int32], [Int64], [Float] and [Bigarray].
- [Marshal].
- [Str] regular expressions.
- [Digest]: MD5 and BLAKE2b.
- {!Workero.Timer}, {!Workero.Date} and {!Workero.Crypto}.
- JavaScript interop with [Js_of_ocaml], for example [JSON].

{1 [jsonkit]}

{{:https://github.com/melange-community/jsonkit}jsonkit} reads and writes JSON,
with a ppx that derives the functions. {!Workero.JSON} builds on it and gives
values as [Jsonkit.t]. It does not re-export jsonkit. opam installs jsonkit with
workero. Add [jsonkit] to the [libraries] of your [dune] file to use it. See
{{!page-json}JSON}.

{1 Server-side React}

[examples/react] renders a page from [.mlx] components with a trimmed copy of
server-reason-react. It uses the synchronous render path only. This example
builds but is not part of the repository's [workerd] test suite.

{1 Embedded files}

A Worker has no file system. To read a file at run time, embed it with the
wasm_of_ocaml [--file] flag. The program reads it with [open_in]:

{@dune[
(executable
 (name main)
 (modes wasm)
 (libraries workero)
 (link_deps motd.txt)
 (wasm_of_ocaml
  (flags
   (--file motd.txt:/static/motd.txt))))
]}

{1 Libraries that need native code}

A library with C stubs that have no wasm implementation fails the build.
[workero build] lists the missing functions. Provide a wasm implementation with
[(wasm_of_ocaml (wasm_files ...))], or drop the library. See {{!page-cli}the
CLI}.

{1 Differences from native OCaml}

- [Sys.word_size] is 32, and [int] has 31 bits.
- The program has no threads or sub-processes. It can open only outbound TCP
  connections, with {!Workero.Socket}.

Successful compilation does not prove that the runtime dependencies of a
library are available in a Worker. See {{!page-testing}Testing a worker}.
